#### Overview

## How do you make an office say who works in it?

The faculty of the Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies (AIS) invited me to collaborate on an office renovation. My brief was to refresh the brand of its Division of Integrative Systems and Design (ISD) and translate the division's story into large-scale wallpaper, in the two months from May to June 2026.

#### Problem

## A logo cannot cover a wall.

A logo works small and at a glance. A wall is seen every day, from across a corridor and from a step away. ISD needed a system that could repeat, scale up to a room and still mean something up close.

#### Approach

## Everything grows from one dot.

I took the dot from the core geometry of the ISD logo and anchored the entire system on it. Three rules shaped every layout:

{% points %}
{% point title="Dots" text="The basic unit, taken from the logo: people in ISD connect the way the dots do." /%}

{% point title="Breath" text="A restrained composition for an ambient space, so the layout breathes and flows." /%}

{% point title="Storyline" text="Patterns set in a deliberate sequence that invites people to pause and read." /%}
{% /points %}

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-1.webp)

A single dot is one person. Set side by side, dots form a shape. Given different sizes, they show that every person brings a different strength.

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-2.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-3.webp)

When different dots come together, they make a pattern no other group has: a fingerprint, the DNA of ISD.

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-4.webp)

#### Storyline

## The story is told in four chapters.

{% points %}
{% point title="Diverse" text="A global collective from many cultural backgrounds." /%}

{% point title="Connect" text="Unique perspectives converge and radiate like ripples." /%}

{% point title="Unite" text="Distinct energies merge into one ripple: a shared vision." /%}

{% point title="Action" text="Layered halftone silhouettes of a team sprinting together." /%}
{% /points %}

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-5.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-6.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-7.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-8.webp)

#### Graphics

## Each chapter also stands on its own.

Taken out of the sequence, every chapter works as a single graphic, ready for a wall, a screen or print.

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-9.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-10.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-11.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-12.webp)

#### Stamps

## The same dots work at the size of a stamp.

Series 1 celebrates ISD itself: founded in 2017, ISD Works, and Innovation, Design, Tech. Series 2 turns the four chapters into a numbered set of four.

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-13.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-14.webp)

#### In the space

## From the screen to the wall.

In AI mockups of the renovated office, the dots run along the corridor past every door and gather around the ISD mark at the entrance.

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-15.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-16.webp)

The Series 1 stamps also went to work as photo props at the HKUST InnoBay Bootcamp.

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-17.webp)

![](/images/experience/hkust-ais/image-18.webp)
